## 1. Using the `Set` Object (The Modern & Easiest Way)

The `Set` object in JavaScript lets you store unique values of any type. This is generally the most concise and idiomatic way to remove duplicates.

**How it works:** You convert the array into a `Set` (which automatically discards duplicates) and then convert it back into an array using the spread syntax (`...`).

```javascript
const arrayWithDuplicates = [1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 4, 5, 1];

// 1. Create a new Set from the array to get unique values
const uniqueSet = new Set(arrayWithDuplicates);

// 2. Convert the Set back into an Array using the spread operator
const uniqueArray = [...uniqueSet];

console.log(uniqueArray); // Output: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
```

